{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AiCt5sh3PSStj77q6xWXKn","type":"tool_result","content":"3340\t    // The agent just touched code. Start the project's own check in a DETACHED\n3341\t    // child and return immediately: a hook that waits for a test suite freezes\n3342\t    // the editor for as long as the suite takes, which is how a supervisor\n3343\t    // becomes the thing people uninstall. The verdict lands in .rabadon/net.json\n3344\t    // and is read on the next hook event — one call of latency, zero stall.\n3345\t    //\n3346\t    // THIS RUNS BEFORE ANY REPORTING, and that ordering is a bug fix, not a\n3347\t    // preference. It used to live below the green->red report, which returns\n3348\t    // early — so the edit that FIXED the breakage never started a check, the\n3349\t    // verdict stayed red, and the refusal it caused could only be cleared by\n3350\t    // making a second, pointless edit. The supervisor had made its own red\n3351\t    // un-clearable. Nothing that reports may sit in front of the thing that\n3352\t    // re-measures.\n3353\t    //\n3354\t    // ENFORCE ONLY. In watch mode rabadon spends not one cycle of the user's\n3355\t    // machine on their repo; watch observes what the agent did, nothing more.\n3356\t    // Turning it on is the moment you accept the cost of being supervised.\n3357\t    bool wantCheck = false, walkCapped = false;\n3358\t    if (toolName == \"Edit\" || toolName == \"Write\" || toolName == \"MultiEdit\") {\n3359\t      // isCode: guard.codePaths present ? ANY match : true.\n3360\t      bool isCodeEdit = true;\n3361\t      if (!guardRaw.empty() && guardRaw.find(\"\\\"codePaths\\\"\") != string::npos) {\n3362\t        isCodeEdit = false;\n3363\t        for (const auto& pat : parse_str_array(guardRaw, \"codePaths\"))\n3364\t          if (rx_test(pat, filePath)) { isCodeEdit = true; break; }\n3365\t      }\n3366\t      wantCheck = isCodeEdit;\n3367\t    } else if (g_mode == MODE_ENFORCE) {\n3368\t      // EVERY OTHER TOOL, asked of the filesystem rather than of the tool name.\n3369\t      // A shell command that wrote a file is an edit; an agent with no edit tool\n3370\t      // makes ALL of its edits this way. Bounded, and the bound is spoken about\n3371\t      // below rather than hidden.\n3372\t      int cap = 20000;\n3373\t      { const char* c = getenv(\"RABADON_WALK_CAP\"); if (c && *c) cap = atoi(c); }\n3374\t      wantCheck = tree_changed_since(cwd, stt.lastNetTs, cap, &walkCapped);\n3375\t    }\n3376\t\n3377\t    if (wantCheck && g_mode == MODE_ENFORCE) {\n3378\t      const string netBin = self_dir() + \"/rabadon-net\";\n3379\t      if (file_exists(netBin)) {\n3380\t        pid_t k = fork();\n3381\t        if (k == 0) {\n3382\t          setsid();\n3383\t          int devnull = open(\"/dev/null\", O_RDWR);\n3384\t          if (devnull >= 0) { dup2(devnull, 0); dup2(devnull, 1); dup2(devnull, 2); }\n3385\t          // argv[0] must carry the FULL path: rabadon-net locates its sibling\n3386\t          // rabadon-truth from it, and a bare name makes it look in the\n3387\t          // supervised project instead of the install directory.\n3388\t          execl(netBin.c_str(), netBin.c_str(), cwd.c_str(), (char*)nullptr);\n3389\t          _exit(127);"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0192cvfjsyyZKrJXRYLswB6P","session_id":"81910dae-7509-4342-9a27-c75d4f682cbf","uuid":"f571ad89-a68d-4a77-83d6-72a24617bd3c","timestamp":"2026-08-24T13:51:06.809Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Trace counter in observe mode"}
