{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GG6TcbvyohrDVyzBYd8cVt","type":"tool_result","content":"691:// an isolated lab, enforce refused `git push --force origin main` with exit 2,\n1787:    << \"  \\\"newRule\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"kebab-id\\\", \\\"deny\\\": \\\"<JS regex over bash commands>\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"<one line>\\\", \\\"catches\\\": [\\\"<the exact command that would have been refused>\\\"], \\\"allow\\\": [\\\"<a real command this must NOT refuse>\\\"] } | { \\\"id\\\": \\\"kebab-id\\\", \\\"match\\\": \\\"<JS regex over file paths>\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"<one line>\\\", \\\"catches\\\": [\\\"<the exact path that would have been protected>\\\"], \\\"allow\\\": [\\\"<a real path this must NOT protect>\\\"] } | null }\\n\"\n1789:    << \"catches is REQUIRED and it is checked. Write the literal command or path this rule would have refused, and rabadon runs it through your own pattern with the same matcher the gate uses before installing anything. A rule whose pattern cannot refuse its own example is not installed, because a rule that reads correctly and refuses nothing is worse than no rule: it is a law everyone believes in.\\n\"\n2282:      // that has refused something it should not have has to carry that too, on\n2339:          const bool refused = isCommand ? rbrules::rx_test_cmd(pat, example)\n2341:          if (refused) {\n2359:    // refuse. 16 refused nothing, in any repository, ever, and all 16 linted\n2386:          const bool refused = isCommand ? rbrules::rx_test_cmd(pat, example)\n2388:          if (!refused) {\n2492:    // Anybody can publish how many commands they refused. That number means\n3299:      // refused on a suite that never ran there; rename the directory it was\n3764:            // The proposal now has to name what it would have refused, and the\n4208:  // now a fresh install refused nothing. guard.json extends this floor;\n4253:    if (verdict.refused) block(verdict.id, verdict.why, verdict.detail);\n4422:  // moment the check is re-run, and re-running the check is never refused.\n4438:    // the obvious thing to type — was refused, and the escape hatch was shut\n4445:    // `npm install left-pad` carries only one and is still refused, which is\n4646:                        \"(recorded with `rabadon wrong`). The next one is refused again.\\n\");","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0192cvfjsyyZKrJXRYLswB6P","session_id":"81910dae-7509-4342-9a27-c75d4f682cbf","uuid":"1cdf78b9-0a7b-4f9e-9f37-75c210e81981","timestamp":"2026-08-24T13:51:31.866Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Trace counter in observe mode"}
