{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0192cvfjsyyZKrJXRYLswB6P","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now let me compile my final answer with the precise file:line evidence:\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Question 1: How is `chains_cut` computed? Which ledger event types increment it?**\n\n`chains_cut` counts both INJECT events and chain-ending STOP events. In `gate.cpp` lines 2036-2046, the code iterates through ledger entries and counts:\n- INJECT events: added to `cuts` vector\n- STOP events: added to `cuts` vector only when a chain is \"open\" (a SIGNAL preceded it)\n\nThen at line 2055: `c.chains_cut = (long long)cuts.size();`\n\nSource: `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:2036-2055`\n\n**Question 2: In OBSERVE/WATCH mode, does the gate still emit INJECT/STOP events? Or only `wouldRefuse` records?**\n\nINJECT events ARE emitted in all modes (no mode check): `gate.cpp:4697-4729` checks only `hook == \"PreToolUse\" && rbinject::enabled()` — **no g_mode condition**.\n\nSTOP events ARE emitted ONLY in ENFORCE mode:\n- Rule violations: `gate.cpp:4100` has explicit `if (g_mode == MODE_ENFORCE)` before STOP emission\n- Budget cap: `gate.cpp:4172` emits STOP unconditionally (always halts), but it's inside a budget check block (not mode-gated)\n\nTherefore: **In WATCH mode, INJECT events ARE emitted but STOP (rule violation) events are NOT.** This means `chains_cut` would NOT be 0 because INJECT events still count.\n\nSources: \n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:4697-4729` (INJECT, no mode check)\n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:4100-4104` (STOP, only if MODE_ENFORCE)\n\n**Question 3: Where is COUNTER written? Which hook event triggers it?**\n\nThe COUNTER event is written in `gate.cpp:4001` via `em.emit(\"COUNTER\", ...)` within the `close_counter()` lambda. This is triggered by two hooks:\n- `SessionEnd` hook: line 4008\n- `Stop` hook: line 4015 (fallback)\n\nBoth call `close_counter()`. A headless `claude -p` run would trigger Stop hook if it's configured as a hook event.\n\nSource: `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:3995-4015`\n\n**Question 4: Any code that emits `estimated_saved` or TOKEN-denominated savings?**\n\nNOT FOUND. Comprehensive grep across all `.h`, `.cpp`, `.mjs`, `.js` files returned no results for:\n- `estimated_saved`\n- `token` + `sav` patterns\n- `sav` + `token` patterns\n\nThe only savings metric is `saved_usd` (USD-denominated, not token-denominated) in `counter.h:77`.\n\nSource: Grep result returned empty for all TOKEN-denominated savings fields."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81910dae-7509-4342-9a27-c75d4f682cbf","uuid":"4f359a6a-fe2d-48f6-a972-872300a77893","timestamp":"2026-08-24T13:51:51.385Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Repo: /Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2 (C++ in native/, JS hook in hooks/gate.mjs).\n\nAnswer these 4 questions with FILE:LINE evidence. Do not speculate — if you cannot find it, say NOT FOUND.\n\n1. How is `chains_cut` computed for the session-close COUNTER event? Which ledger event types increment it? (counter.h comment says \"INJECT and chain-ending STOP events\"). Find the actual code that counts them.\n\n2. rabadon has modes: watch/observe (records \"wouldRefuse\", enforces nothing) vs on/enforce. In OBSERVE/WATCH mode, does the gate still emit INJECT events and chain-ending STOP events? Or does observe mode produce ONLY `wouldRefuse` records with no INJECT/STOP? This is the critical question: in observe mode, would `chains_cut` be structurally 0?\n\n3. Where is the COUNTER event actually written (which source file/function, triggered by which hook event, e.g. SessionEnd/Stop)? Does a headless `claude -p` run trigger it?\n\n4. Is there ANY code path anywhere in the repo that emits a field literally named `estimated_saved`, or any TOKEN-denominated (not USD) savings estimate? Search all of native/, hooks/, bin/, index.mjs, repair/, npm/.\n\nReturn a compact answer, max ~20 lines, with file:line citations. No file dumps.","agentId":"a930ee9bc283dd46d","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now let me compile my final answer with the precise file:line evidence:\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Question 1: How is `chains_cut` computed? Which ledger event types increment it?**\n\n`chains_cut` counts both INJECT events and chain-ending STOP events. In `gate.cpp` lines 2036-2046, the code iterates through ledger entries and counts:\n- INJECT events: added to `cuts` vector\n- STOP events: added to `cuts` vector only when a chain is \"open\" (a SIGNAL preceded it)\n\nThen at line 2055: `c.chains_cut = (long long)cuts.size();`\n\nSource: `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:2036-2055`\n\n**Question 2: In OBSERVE/WATCH mode, does the gate still emit INJECT/STOP events? Or only `wouldRefuse` records?**\n\nINJECT events ARE emitted in all modes (no mode check): `gate.cpp:4697-4729` checks only `hook == \"PreToolUse\" && rbinject::enabled()` — **no g_mode condition**.\n\nSTOP events ARE emitted ONLY in ENFORCE mode:\n- Rule violations: `gate.cpp:4100` has explicit `if (g_mode == MODE_ENFORCE)` before STOP emission\n- Budget cap: `gate.cpp:4172` emits STOP unconditionally (always halts), but it's inside a budget check block (not mode-gated)\n\nTherefore: **In WATCH mode, INJECT events ARE emitted but STOP (rule violation) events are NOT.** This means `chains_cut` would NOT be 0 because INJECT events still count.\n\nSources: \n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:4697-4729` (INJECT, no mode check)\n- `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:4100-4104` (STOP, only if MODE_ENFORCE)\n\n**Question 3: Where is COUNTER written? Which hook event triggers it?**\n\nThe COUNTER event is written in `gate.cpp:4001` via `em.emit(\"COUNTER\", ...)` within the `close_counter()` lambda. This is triggered by two hooks:\n- `SessionEnd` hook: line 4008\n- `Stop` hook: line 4015 (fallback)\n\nBoth call `close_counter()`. A headless `claude -p` run would trigger Stop hook if it's configured as a hook event.\n\nSource: `/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp:3995-4015`\n\n**Question 4: Any code that emits `estimated_saved` or TOKEN-denominated savings?**\n\nNOT FOUND. Comprehensive grep across all `.h`, `.cpp`, `.mjs`, `.js` files returned no results for:\n- `estimated_saved`\n- `token` + `sav` patterns\n- `sav` + `token` patterns\n\nThe only savings metric is `saved_usd` (USD-denominated, not token-denominated) in `counter.h:77`.\n\nSource: Grep result returned empty for all TOKEN-denominated savings fields."}],"totalDurationMs":66075,"totalTokens":42399,"totalToolUseCount":32,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":41324,"output_tokens":811,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":41324,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":17,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
